#: ../../layers/normalizations/batch_renormalization.rst:3
msgid "Batch Renormalization"
msgstr ""

#: marquetry.layers.normalize.batch_renormalization.BatchRenormalization:1 of
msgid "Batch renormalization layer."
msgstr ""

#: marquetry.layers.normalize.batch_renormalization.BatchRenormalization:3 of
msgid ""
"Batch renormalization extends batch normalization so that train-time "
"normalization stays close to the inference-time normalization even with "
"small or non-i.i.d. mini-batches. The batch statistics are corrected "
"toward the running statistics by the clipped factors ``r`` and ``d``."
msgstr ""

#: marquetry.layers.normalize.batch_renormalization.BatchRenormalization:8 of
msgid ""
"With ``rmax=1`` and ``dmax=0`` (default), the behavior is identical to "
":class:`marquetry.layers.BatchNormalization`. The paper suggests starting"
" the training with the defaults and gradually relaxing the bounds (e.g. "
"``rmax`` toward 3 and ``dmax`` toward 5)."
msgstr ""

#: marquetry.layers.normalize.batch_renormalization.BatchRenormalization of
msgid "Parameters"
msgstr ""

#: marquetry.layers.normalize.batch_renormalization.BatchRenormalization:13 of
msgid ""
"The clipping bound of the std correction factor ``r``. Default is 1.0 (no"
" correction)."
msgstr ""

#: marquetry.layers.normalize.batch_renormalization.BatchRenormalization:16 of
msgid ""
"The clipping bound of the mean correction factor ``d``. Default is 0.0 "
"(no correction)."
msgstr ""

#: marquetry.layers.normalize.batch_renormalization.BatchRenormalization:19 of
msgid ""
"The weighting factor for the moving averages of mean and variance. "
"Default is 0.9."
msgstr ""

#: marquetry.layers.normalize.batch_renormalization.BatchRenormalization:22 of
msgid "A small constant value preventing zero-division. Default is 1e-15."
msgstr ""

#: marquetry.layers.normalize.batch_renormalization.BatchRenormalization:28 of
msgid "The gamma parameter used for scaling."
msgstr ""

#: marquetry.layers.normalize.batch_renormalization.BatchRenormalization of
msgid "type"
msgstr ""

#: marquetry.layers.normalize.batch_renormalization.BatchRenormalization:30
#: marquetry.layers.normalize.batch_renormalization.BatchRenormalization:36
#: marquetry.layers.normalize.batch_renormalization.BatchRenormalization:42
#: marquetry.layers.normalize.batch_renormalization.BatchRenormalization:48 of
msgid "marquetry.Parameter"
msgstr ""

#: marquetry.layers.normalize.batch_renormalization.BatchRenormalization:34 of
msgid "The beta parameter used for shifting."
msgstr ""

#: marquetry.layers.normalize.batch_renormalization.BatchRenormalization:40 of
msgid "The moving average of the mean."
msgstr ""

#: marquetry.layers.normalize.batch_renormalization.BatchRenormalization:46 of
msgid "The moving average of the variance."
msgstr ""

